---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import { legal } from "../../data/legal";
---
<BaseLayout lang="en" title="Privacy policy | CongTrinhSnap" description={`How ${legal.appName} and this website collect, use, store and protect personal data.`}>
<SiteHeader /><main id="main">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Legal</span><h1>Privacy policy</h1><p>Effective date: {legal.effectiveDate}.</p></div></section>
<article class="prose">
<p>This policy applies to the Android app <strong>{legal.appName}</strong> (device name: {legal.appLauncherName}, package: <code>{legal.packageName}</code>) and the website <a href={legal.siteUrl}>{legal.siteUrl.replace("https://", "")}</a>. The service provider and personal data controller is <strong>{legal.legalName}</strong>, an individual who develops and operates the product under the <strong>{legal.brandName}</strong> brand (“we”, “us”). DoS Studio is a brand, not a separate legal entity.</p>
<h2>1. Information we process</h2>
<h3>1.1. Use without signing in</h3><p>Project information, photos, videos, drawings, documents and notes are stored on your device. Under the app's described design, we do not receive information stored only locally. If you use the Free plan, advertising SDKs may process technical information as described in section 1.7.</p>
<h3>1.2. Google account</h3><p>When you sign in, the app processes your email address, display name, Google profile photo (if provided) and Firebase user ID for authentication, synchronization, project sharing and Pro-plan management.</p>
<h3>1.3. Synchronized project data</h3><ul><li>Project details and text, such as names, addresses, dates, members, roles, notes, photo captions and creation/update times, are stored in Google Cloud Firestore.</li><li>Photos, videos, drawings and documents are encrypted on your device before upload to the app folder in the uploader's Google Drive.</li><li>Invitations may include the invitee's email, role, inviter, status and expiry.</li></ul><p>Projects marked “On this device only” are not synchronized to the server under the current design.</p>
<h3>1.4. Location and GPS photo stamps</h3><p>Only when you grant location permission and actively enable GPS stamping does the app read coordinates to place them on a captured photo. Coordinates become part of the image and may be synchronized with it if you sync the project. The app is not described as actively tracking background location. Location linked to an individual may be sensitive personal data. Enable this feature only if you understand and agree that coordinates may appear on shared images.</p>
<h3>1.5. Device information</h3><p>When signed in, the app may process the Android device identifier (ANDROID_ID), manufacturer, model, Android version and app version to enforce Pro device limits, detect abuse and provide technical support.</p>
<h3>1.6. Purchases and Pro</h3><p>Google Play processes payments; we do not receive your payment card number. The app receives transaction status and stores a SHA-256 hashed transaction identifier associated with your account to verify Pro entitlement and prevent fraud. A hashed identifier is not necessarily anonymous if it can still be linked to an account or transaction.</p>
<h3>1.7. Advertising on Free</h3><p>The app displays ads through Appodeal and integrated advertising partners, which may include BidMachine. Depending on SDKs, configuration and your consent choices, these providers may process Advertising ID, IP address, device information, interaction data and approximate location to deliver, frequency-cap and measure ads. You can manage Advertising ID and ad settings in Android settings. Pro is described as ad-free. See the <a href="https://www.appodeal.com/privacy-policy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Appodeal Privacy Policy</a> and the policies of relevant ad networks.</p>
<h3>1.8. Support communications</h3><p>If you email us, we process your email address, message and attachments to respond, troubleshoot and handle complaints.</p>
<h2>2. Purposes and legal grounds</h2><ul><li>Provide sign-in, storage, synchronization, sharing, report export and features you request.</li><li>Manage accounts, verify Pro, enforce device limits, prevent fraud and protect the service.</li><li>Deliver advertising on Free subject to applicable consent choices and mechanisms.</li><li>Respond to support requests, resolve disputes and comply with legal obligations.</li></ul><p>We do not sell personal data. Where the law requires consent, we will request it before processing. You may withdraw consent using the process in section 8. Withdrawal does not affect the lawfulness of processing carried out before withdrawal.</p>
<h2>3. Encryption and access</h2><ul><li>Synchronized project files are encrypted on the device using AES-256-GCM before upload to Google Drive, according to the current technical design.</li><li>Project decryption keys are stored in Firestore and made available to members according to access rights. Administrators have technical privileges over the Firestore database; this is therefore not end-to-end encryption, and we do not claim that administrators are technically unable to access keys.</li><li>Firestore text data is not additionally encrypted by the app under the current description; Google applies encryption in transit and at rest as described in its service documentation.</li><li>Project members may view information according to assigned roles. Share projects only with authorized people.</li></ul>
<h2>4. Recipients and processors</h2><ul><li><strong>Google:</strong> Firebase Authentication, Cloud Firestore, Google Drive, Google Sign-In and Google Play for authentication, storage, synchronization and payments.</li><li><strong>Appodeal and integrated ad networks:</strong> process advertising-related information on Free according to the actual SDKs and configuration.</li><li><strong>Project members:</strong> people you invite or who invite you, within their assigned roles and permissions.</li><li><strong>OpenAI:</strong> only when you select “Ask AI” and confirm the transfer. The described workflow sends the currently viewed drawing-region image and your question to the ChatGPT app on your device; you use your own ChatGPT account. Subsequent processing is subject to OpenAI's terms and privacy policy. We do not claim to control OpenAI's subsequent processing.</li><li><strong>Third-party DWG conversion website:</strong> the app opens a conversion page in your browser. Processing of files and technical data, including whether files are transmitted to the provider's servers, depends on that website's operation. Review its privacy policy and terms before uploading. We do not control processing after you leave the app to use that service.</li><li><strong>Apps you choose to share with:</strong> for example, Zalo, Gmail or Drive when you actively export or share a file.</li><li><strong>Competent authorities:</strong> where there is a lawful basis and valid request.</li></ul>
<h2>5. Storage and international transfers</h2><p>Google, Appodeal and advertising networks may process or store data on infrastructure outside Vietnam, depending on their configurations and terms. Use of these providers may involve cross-border transfers of personal data. We will carry out impact assessment, documentation and notification/filing obligations as required by applicable law. The specific storage country may depend on provider service regions and account settings.</p>
<h2>6. Retention</h2><ul><li>Cloud account, device and project data are retained as needed to provide the service, until you delete the data/account or another lawful basis for retention applies.</li><li>Deleted items may remain in the app trash for up to 7 days under the current mechanism before permanent deletion.</li><li>You manage files in your Google Drive; deletion requests depend on access rights and your choices in the app.</li><li>Hashed transaction identifiers are retained as needed for transaction verification, subscription management and fraud prevention, then reviewed for deletion or de-linking unless legally required.</li><li>Support emails are retained as needed to handle requests, complaints, protect legitimate interests or comply with law.</li></ul>
<h2>7. Account and data deletion</h2><p>You can request deletion in the app or through the <a href="/en/delete-account">Delete account and data</a> page. That page explains the steps, data affected, possible retention and processing periods. Some information held by Google or other third parties may require a separate request to that provider.</p>
<h2>8. Your rights and how to exercise them</h2><p>Under Vietnam's Personal Data Protection Law No. 91/2025/QH15 and implementing regulations, you may exercise rights provided by law, including rights to be informed, consent or withdraw consent, access and correct, request provision, deletion or restriction, object to processing, complain, report and seek compensation where applicable.</p><p>Send your request to <a href={`mailto:${legal.supportEmail}`}>{legal.supportEmail}</a> from the email linked to your account, or provide information reasonably needed to verify your identity and the scope of the request. Do not send passwords or one-time codes. Verification should not unreasonably obstruct your rights.</p><p>For a valid deletion request, we respond within 2 business days, provide procedural guidance and complete processing within 20 days. Where coordination with processors or third parties is needed, processing may take 30 days. If complexity requires an extension, we may extend once by no more than 20 days, explain the reason and be able to demonstrate that the extension is necessary and reasonable. Lawful exceptions or mandatory retention will be explained. These periods follow Article 5 of Decree 356/2025/ND-CP and applicable law.</p><p>Other rights are handled within the timeframes and procedures applicable under current law. If a request cannot be fulfilled for a legitimate reason or a lawful refusal ground applies, we will explain the reason to the extent permitted.</p>
<h2>9. Security and incidents</h2><p>We use technical and organizational measures appropriate to the service, including access controls, Firestore security rules and file encryption as described in section 3. No system can guarantee absolute security. If an incident occurs, we will handle it and notify authorities/affected individuals within the timeframes and procedures required by law. For violations involving location or biometric data, notification to affected data subjects is made within no more than 72 hours after discovery where required by applicable rules.</p>
<h2>10. Children</h2><p>The app is designed for construction project management and is not specifically designed for children. If you believe a child's data has been provided unlawfully, contact us so we can review and respond under applicable law.</p>
<h2>11. Website</h2><p>The website does not provide user accounts or store project records. Cloudflare, the hosting provider, may process technical data such as IP address, browser information and access logs to operate and protect the website under its <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy Policy</a>. If analytics, cookies or tracking technologies are added, we will update this policy and the relevant notice/consent mechanism before activation.</p>
<h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2><p>We may update this policy to reflect service or legal changes. Updates will be posted here with an effective date; material changes will be communicated in the app or through an appropriate channel.</p>
<h2>13. Contact</h2><p><strong>{legal.legalName}</strong> – operating under the <strong>{legal.brandName}</strong> brand<br />Email: <a href={`mailto:${legal.supportEmail}`}>{legal.supportEmail}</a></p>
<p><strong>Language notice:</strong> This English translation is provided for convenience. If there is any inconsistency, the Vietnamese version prevails for interpretation in Vietnam.</p>
</article></main><SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
